(198908, 11202, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met, and creative.  centering your subject works well here, the cheese, straw and the decorative glitzy thing break up the symmetry well, and help balance the overall shot.  i like the colors, and that you have echoed them in the frame (especially the thin red line), but, personally, i think the yellow part of it is just a little too wide.  your focus and colors are good, one other (very minor) nitpick would be that the shadow is cropped a tad at the side, it''s so little that it looks accidental.  either crop it more or keep it all in, i think, especially since you have such a plain background that the shadow is pretty noticeable.  overall, i really like your photo, sebastian :)</td>', 'challenge met, and creative.  centering your subject works well here, the cheese, straw and the decorative glitzy thing break up the symmetry well, and help balance the overall shot.  i like the colors, and that you have echoed them in the frame (especially the thin red line), but, personally, i think the yellow part of it is just a little too wide.  your focus and colors are good, one other (very minor) nitpick would be that the shadow is cropped a tad at the side, it''s so little that it looks accidental.  either crop it more or keep it all in, i think, especially since you have such a plain background that the shadow is pretty noticeable.  overall, i really like your photo, sebastian :)', '2003-01-23 17:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(198909, 11162, 1041, '<td valign="top">this is a powerful concept that definitely meets the challenge.  the red works well here and i think your frame complements the photo well.  composition-wise, this is also good, just enough visible of the strawberry so that the viewer can easily identify it.  the strawberry looks a little grainy or out of focus to me though, and i''m not totally sure about the strong shadow from the light or flash.  i guess you need some to be able to see the "splash" part, and i''m not sure how easy it would''ve been (if indeed possible) to tone the shadow down w/out loosing the visibility of the splash.  good photo :)</td>', 'this is a powerful concept that definitely meets the challenge.  the red works well here and i think your frame complements the photo well.  composition-wise, this is also good, just enough visible of the strawberry so that the viewer can easily identify it.  the strawberry looks a little grainy or out of focus to me though, and i''m not totally sure about the strong shadow from the light or flash.  i guess you need some to be able to see the "splash" part, and i''m not sure how easy it would''ve been (if indeed possible) to tone the shadow down w/out loosing the visibility of the splash.  good photo :)', '2003-01-23 17:57:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(198914, 11341, 1041, '<td valign="top">this is a really creative idea that meets the challenge well.  the photo''s nice and sharp, too, but your lighting is too uneven for my liking and distracts from the photo overall.  it looks as if you used a very strong light, i wonder if you are one of the growing DPC community that use workman lights.  i have those and have found that they give me very nice and even lighting if i put the camera on a tripod and hold a white bedsheet between the light and the subject of the photo.  another nitpick would be that the mouse cable seems clipped just a little bit on the left.  either crop more of it out or keep it all in, this way it looks a little accidental to me.  probably keep it all in in this case because i like the curve of it through the picture.  overall, a decent and creative photo :)</td>', 'this is a really creative idea that meets the challenge well.  the photo''s nice and sharp, too, but your lighting is too uneven for my liking and distracts from the photo overall.  it looks as if you used a very strong light, i wonder if you are one of the growing DPC community that use workman lights.  i have those and have found that they give me very nice and even lighting if i put the camera on a tripod and hold a white bedsheet between the light and the subject of the photo.  another nitpick would be that the mouse cable seems clipped just a little bit on the left.  either crop more of it out or keep it all in, this way it looks a little accidental to me.  probably keep it all in in this case because i like the curve of it through the picture.  overall, a decent and creative photo :)', '2003-01-23 18:00:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(198928, 11168, 4055, '<td valign="top">I like it very much. The colours are good and the focus is perfect. The composition is very nice with the building at left. I have a feeling that the photo is leaning a litlle to the right when I look at the horizon,  but when I check the building it doesn´t seem to be so. Overall a very nice shot. High score´s coming.</td>', 'I like it very much. The colours are good and the focus is perfect. The composition is very nice with the building at left. I have a feeling that the photo is leaning a litlle to the right when I look at the horizon,  but when I check the building it doesn´t seem to be so. Overall a very nice shot. High score´s coming.', '2003-01-23 18:24:54.000000', NULL, 1),
